  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media Council of Tanzania, MCT - Media Council of Tanzania</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Media Council of Tanzania, MCT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall Outcome for MCT Strategic Plan The environment for media/press freedom and freedom of expression is enhanced and defended and the media are accountable while exercising their rights enabling them to provide the public with diverse information and views in a professional manner. 

 Outcomes for the areas for Swedish support
 - Outcome 1 Advocacy for repeal and review of anti-media laws - Concerted efforts by media and political stakeholders to make current media and other laws and regulations more media-friendly and accountable to press freedom 
 - Outcome 3 Arbitration MCT Arbitration of complaints is improved and widely accepted by public and the media</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sverige har varit med att fr&#xe5;n b&#xf6;rjan bygga upp Tanzanias medier&#xe5;d vilken fyller en viktig demokratisk funktion i landet. R&#xe5;det &#xe4;gs av medierna sj&#xe4;lva och &#xe4;r en frivillig instans dit allm&#xe4;nheten kan v&#xe4;nda sig med klagom&#xe5;l. MCT medlar, arbetar med medieetik och p&#xe5;verkansarbete. Denna insats st&#xf6;der ett projekt som framf&#xf6;rallt &#xe4;mnar att st&#xe4;rka pressfrihet, yttrandefrihet och medieetik. En del av projektet &#xe4;r inriktat p&#xe5; p&#xe5;verkansarbete f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra den nuvarande och kommande medialagstiftningen p&#xe5; fastlandet och p&#xe5; Zanzibar. Detta arbete g&#xf6;rs i n&#xe4;ra samarbete med en rad nationella, regionala och internationella partnerorganisationer och n&#xe4;tverk, samt i dialog med regeringen p&#xe5; fastlandet och Zanzibar. Den andra delen av projektet fokuserar p&#xe5; &#xf6;kad mediaprofessionalism och ansvarstagande av medier och journalister. MCT vill uppn&#xe5; detta genom forts&#xe4;tta och &#xf6;kat fr&#xe4;mjande av sj&#xe4;lvregulation av medier och organisationens medlingsarbete som ska g&#xf6;ras mer k&#xe4;nt f&#xf6;r allm&#xe4;nheten i hela Tanzania.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sweden has been part of building up the Media Council of Tanzania from the outset, which fills an important democratic function in the country. The council is owned by the media itself and is a voluntary body the public can turn to in order to file complaints against media. MCT mediates, works with media ethics and advocacy work. This initiative supports a project aimed primarily at strengthening freedom of the press, freedom of expression and media ethics. Part of the project focuses on efforts to improve current and future media legislation in the mainland and Zanzibar. This work is being done in close cooperation with a number of national, regional and international partner organizations and networks, as well as in dialogue with the government on the mainland and Zanzibar. The second part of the project focuses on increased media professionalism and ethics of media and journalists. MCT wants to achieve this by continuing and increasing the promotion of self-regulation of media and the organization&apos;s mediation work, which will be made more widely known to the public throughout Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
